#
# Counter-example for the reasoned-graph math: expression-identity gate
# (crates/logic/src/math_expression.rs, check_structural_key_on_rejected_expression):
# ex:app is a math:ApplicationExpression missing its required math:operator — the
# math: expression lowering REJECTS it — yet it carries an authored math:structuralKey,
# claiming a structural identity for a thing the grammar itself refutes. The gate MUST
# raise math:StructuralKeyOnRejectedExpression (and neither of its two siblings
# math:StructuralKeyDrift / math:SurfaceLeakInNormalForm).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:app a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:structuralKey "whatever" .
